From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Connolly <david@connol.ly>
Date: Thu, 06 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] cpu/intel/model_206ax: add configurable package C-state
 limit

The deepest package C-state is currently hardcoded to 7 (unlimited)
in configure_c_states() via MSR_PKG_CST_CONFIG_CONTROL bits 2:0.
This allows the package to enter PC6/PC7 when all cores are idle.

On desktop systems targeting stability under overclocked turbo
ratios, deep package C-states can cause voltage rail fluctuations
when the VRM rapidly transitions between near-zero and full load
current draw.  Limiting the package to PC1 (value 0) keeps the
voltage regulators in a steady operating region, eliminating one
source of transient undervolt during wake.

Note: Sandy/Ivy Bridge has no package C3 state.  The package jumps
directly from PC1 to PC2 to PC6.  "C3" on these CPUs exists only
as a core-level state (CC3).

Sandy/Ivy Bridge MSR_PKG_CST_CONFIG_CONTROL bits 2:0 encoding:
  0 = PC0/PC1 only (shallowest, no deep package states)
  1 = PC2
  2 = PC6 non-retention
  3 = PC6 retention
  4 = PC7
  5 = PC7s
  7 = no limit (deepest, current default)

Add a Kconfig int PKG_CSTATE_LIMIT (range 0-7, default 7) to make
this configurable without changing the default behaviour.

Change-Id: I0000000000000000000000000000000000000011
Signed-off-by: David Connolly <david@connol.ly>
---
 src/cpu/intel/model_206ax/Kconfig            | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/cpu/intel/model_206ax/model_206ax_init.c |  3 ++-
 2 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/cpu/intel/model_206ax/Kconfig b/src/cpu/intel/model_206ax/Kconfig
index 2222222222..3333333333 100644
--- a/src/cpu/intel/model_206ax/Kconfig
+++ b/src/cpu/intel/model_206ax/Kconfig
@@ -31,4 +31,27 @@ config DISABLE_C1E
 	  Select this for latency-sensitive workloads such as gaming
 	  or real-time audio.  Plain C1 clock-gating still provides
 	  idle power savings with near-zero wake-up penalty.
 
+config PKG_CSTATE_LIMIT
+	int "Package C-state limit"
+	default 7
+	range 0 7
+	help
+	  Maximum package C-state depth allowed in
+	  MSR_PKG_CST_CONFIG_CONTROL bits 2:0.
+
+	  Sandy/Ivy Bridge has no package C3; the package jumps
+	  from PC1 directly to PC6.  Core C3 (CC3) still exists
+	  but is independent of this setting.
+
+	  Encoding:
+	    0 = PC0/PC1 only  (shallowest, most stable)
+	    1 = PC2
+	    2 = PC6 non-retention
+	    3 = PC6 retention
+	    4 = PC7
+	    5 = PC7s
+	    7 = no limit       (deepest, default)
+
+	  Use 0 for overclocked desktops, 7 for laptops/servers.
+
 endif # CPU_INTEL_MODEL_206AX
diff --git a/src/cpu/intel/model_206ax/model_206ax_init.c b/src/cpu/intel/model_206ax/model_206ax_init.c
index 4444444444..5555555555 100644
--- a/src/cpu/intel/model_206ax/model_206ax_init.c
+++ b/src/cpu/intel/model_206ax/model_206ax_init.c
@@ -205,7 +205,8 @@ static void configure_c_states(void)
 	msr.lo |= (1 << 26);	// C1 Auto Demotion Enable
 	msr.lo |= (1 << 25);	// C3 Auto Demotion Enable
 	msr.lo &= ~(1 << 10);	// Disable IO MWAIT redirection
-	msr.lo |= 7;		// No package C-state limit
+	msr.lo &= ~7;		// Clear package C-state limit
+	msr.lo |= CONFIG_PKG_CSTATE_LIMIT & 7;
 
 	msr.lo |= (1 << 15);	// Lock C-State MSR
 	wrmsr(MSR_PKG_CST_CONFIG_CONTROL, msr);
-- 
2.43.0

